." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-9838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "40da0c475691ba2080c14333da3cae6b5ef76b5dd94b1d63f46d5d19c0e221c7"} {"question" "q-9838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-9838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-9838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-9961" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the determinant of  $[\\begin{aligned}1 & n & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ is $-6$, find the value of $n.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-9961" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & n & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4-n\\cdot 2+0 \\\\  & =4-2n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-6,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-2n & =-6 \\\\ -2n & =-10 \\\\ n & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-9961" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "40da0c475691ba2080c14333da3cae6b5ef76b5dd94b1d63f46d5d19c0e221c7"} {"question" "q-9961" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-9961" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "5"] ["text" "Any real number"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-9961" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-69834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $M$ given below?\n\n- $M$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(M)=1$\n- $det(M)=0$\n\n \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-69834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-4-12)+2(-2+6)+1(4+4) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-16)+2\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =-16+8+8 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(M)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-69834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "40da0c475691ba2080c14333da3cae6b5ef76b5dd94b1d63f46d5d19c0e221c7"} {"question" "q-69834" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-69834" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-69834" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-128506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the determinant of\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & m \\\\ m & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nis $-29$, find all the possible values of $m.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-128506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $m:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & m \\\\ m & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-6|\\begin{aligned}m & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+m|\\begin{aligned}m & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-0)-6(m-0)+m(m-6) \\\\  & =3-6m+{m}^{2}-6m \\\\  & ={m}^{2}-12m+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-29,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-12m+3 & =-29 \\\\ {m}^{2}-12m+32 & =0 \\\\ m & =\\frac{-(-12)\\pm \\sqrt{{12}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 32}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm \\sqrt{16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm 4}{2} \\\\  & =6\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $m=4$ and $m=8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-128506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "40da0c475691ba2080c14333da3cae6b5ef76b5dd94b1d63f46d5d19c0e221c7"} {"question" "q-128506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-128506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$-5$ and $1$ only"] ["text" "$-6$ and $3$ only"] ["text" "$1$ only"] ["text" "$4$ and $8$ only"] ["text" "$8$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-128506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$4$ and $8$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-280400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $W=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ then $det(W)=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-280400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =5|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5(4\\cdot 1-6\\cdot (-3))+2((-1)(1)-6\\cdot 2)+3((-1)(-3)-4\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =5(4+18)+2(-1-12)+3(3-8) \\\\  & =5(22)+2(-13)+3(-5) \\\\  & =110-26-15 \\\\  & =69\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/state.json" "file_sha256" "17174380396c562993de9510e1a2183d70f3291e1ce6cf3aa18f247a279f996b"} {"question" "q-280400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "40da0c475691ba2080c